[1] Fourier-Toeplitz dual lemma
  Let D_S(t)=sum_v 1_{||v t||<1/14} and F_S=D_S-1.
  If S is a strict counterexample, then F_S(t)>=0 a.e.
  Therefore for every polynomial q(t)=sum_{j=0}^K c_j exp(2*pi*i*j*t):
      integral F_S(t) |q(t)|^2 dt >= 0
  Equivalently T_K=(hat F_S(i-j)) is PSD.
  A negative eigenvalue of T_K is a rigorous dual obstruction to covering,
  up to numerical robustness of the displayed eigenvalue.
